<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:52:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>RN 'breach': Amid 'severe' differences with 'bright, young' Bardella, Le Pen 'dictates party line'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260910-rn-breach-amid-severe-differences-with-bright-young-bardella-le-pen-dictates-party-line</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Victor Mallet, Financial Times Senior Editor at the World News Desk. He interprets the emerging tensions between Marine Le Pen and Jordan Bardella as more than a clash of personalities. They reveal a deeper struggle over the political future of France's far-right National Rally is becoming as they find themselves in prime position in their hunt to capture the French presidency. Bardella is formally president of the party and has developed his own political constituency, particularly among younger voters and parts of the business community. Yet Mallet argues that Le Pen continues to exercise the decisive ideological and strategic authority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c52ffaa2-ad13-11f1-bc69-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15977956506aa2a38080bf94-07231205.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c52ffaa2-ad13-11f1-bc69-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15977956506aa2a38080bf94-07231205.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aadc5776-ad14-11f1-bf36-3369797d02fb</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:39:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Algeria cuts diplomatic ties with United Arab Emirates over 'provocative and hostile actions'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260910-algeria-cuts-diplomatic-ties-with-united-arab-emirates-over-provocative-and-hostile-actions</link><description>
Algeria is severing diplomatic ties with the United Arab Emirates, state media reported Thursday. Algerian President ‌Abdelmadjid Tebboune has in the past accused the Gulf state of trying to meddle in Algeria's internal affairs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc05aaf6-ad0b-11f1-83d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25106649315369.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc05aaf6-ad0b-11f1-83d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25106649315369.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5432f6e0-ad0b-11f1-b507-47d8210ea19e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:50:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc05aaf6-ad0b-11f1-83d5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25106649315369.jpg">© Fateh Guidoum, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Colombia court orders President de la Espriella to hide social media videos of him with dead bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-colombia-court-orders-president-de-la-espriella-to-hide-social-media-videos-of-him-with-dead-bodies</link><description>
Colombia's right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella has been ordered to hide social media videos showing him walking past rows of the dead bodies of alleged guerrillas killed by the country's armed forces, according to a court document seen Wednesday. The newly sworn-in president has launched a fresh offensive at armed groups involved in the country's lucrative cocaine trade. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51dbf7c8-acf4-11f1-92e9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238627978322.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51dbf7c8-acf4-11f1-92e9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238627978322.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">744a1a40-acfb-11f1-8727-bfbc394ea958</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:31:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51dbf7c8-acf4-11f1-92e9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238627978322.jpg">© Fernando Vergara, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Rubio in Peru: Protestors take the streets against US Secretary of State's visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-rubio-in-peru-protestors-take-the-streets-against-us-secretary-of-state-s-visit</link><description>
Protesters marched in Lima against the arrival of US Secretary of State Marco Rubio and US policy toward Peru and Latin America, defending the autonomy of countries in the region. "What he has come to do is impose a policy without any kind of consultation, as if Peru were effectively his vassal," explained a woman participating in the march.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/470bcf9c-ad0a-11f1-8f22-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-130648-130815-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/470bcf9c-ad0a-11f1-8f22-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-130648-130815-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c43f7a0-ad0a-11f1-9826-bf209434bc1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:30:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump highlights his own record at midterm Republican convention</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-trump-highlights-his-own-record-at-midterm-republican-convention</link><description>
President Donald Trump capped Wednesday’s opening night of the unusual Republican midterm convention by slamming Democrats as extremists and staunchly defending the war in Iran while making the extraordinary pledge to pay every adult American $5,000 if his party retains its control of both chambers of Congress after November. It reflected Trump’s apparent calculation that he needs bold moves to revive Republicans’ chances as Democrats try to take advantage of his low approval ratings in close races across the country. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington DC.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5bdd470-ad09-11f1-91c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-130251-130506-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d5bdd470-ad09-11f1-91c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-130251-130506-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da7c548c-ad09-11f1-bc18-bf209434bc1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:26:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ethiopia's Tigray rebels accuse govt of new drone strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-ethiopia-s-tigray-rebels-accuse-govt-of-new-drone-strike</link><description>
Rebel Tigrayan authorities accused Ethiopia of another drone strike in the country's northern region on Tuesday. The federal government has launched multiple drone strikes in Tigray in recent weeks and massed troops at the regional border, raising fears of a return to the civil war of 2020-2022 that killed some 600,000 people. FRANCE 24's Tom Canetti reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeefa1b8-ad07-11f1-ac5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-214816-214927-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/aeefa1b8-ad07-11f1-ac5b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-214816-214927-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b41b02ae-ad07-11f1-aee4-bf209434bc1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:23:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Korea to boost artificial intelligence ties with Africa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-south-korea-to-boost-artificial-intelligence-ties-with-africa</link><description>
In Seoul, South Korea, 45 African states have been meeting under the Ministerial conference of the Korea Africa Economic Cooperation. This year's topic is Artificial intelligence, and how those new technologies could be implemented on the African continent. FRANCE 24’s Seoul correspondent, Chloe Borgnon reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb35d442-ad07-11f1-8c8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-215505-215630-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bb35d442-ad07-11f1-8c8d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-215505-215630-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0a3eaea-ad07-11f1-a870-bf209434bc1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:22:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sudan war: Chad denies allegations of logistical support to RSF rebels</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-sudan-war-chad-denies-allegations-of-logistical-support-to-rsf-rebels</link><description>
On Tuesday in Geneva, Chad once again denied any involvement in the war in Sudan, while taking part in the 63rd session of the UN Human Rights Council. N’Djamena has repeatedly been accused of serving as a logistical rear base for Sudan’s Rapid Support Forces and has consistently rejected those allegations. FRANCE 24’s Harold Girard reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5242248-ad07-11f1-b2ef-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-214527-214721-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b5242248-ad07-11f1-b2ef-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-214527-214721-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba347490-ad07-11f1-b32e-9334f92d0470</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:21:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Rwanda positions itself as an African space pioneer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-rwanda-positions-itself-as-an-african-space-pioneer</link><description>
Several African heads of state and leaders of national space agencies, including Rwandan President Paul Kagame, attended  the very first international space summit hosted in France on Thursday. FRANCE 24’s Aurore Bayoud took the opportunity to visit the Rwanda Space Agency, created in 2020.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6770ddc-ad07-11f1-a3df-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-215652-215836-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6770ddc-ad07-11f1-a3df-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260909-215652-215836-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb2fac3a-ad07-11f1-9a4c-bf209434bc1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:20:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>PSG make perfect start to Champions League title defence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260910-psg-make-perfect-start-to-champions-league-title-defence</link><description>
The reigning champions are in fine form. After a poor start to their league campaign, PSG came alive on their return to European action, cruising to a 6-1 win over Slovakian side Slovan Bratislava. Ousmane Dembélé, who scored twice and provided two assists, and Ferran Torres, who hit a hat-trick, led PSG to victory.
 
In the other matches, Liverpool edged past Atlético Madrid 2-1, while Barcelona cruised past Feyenoord 5-1. Last season’s runners-up Arsenal secured a 1-0 win over Napoli.
 
In tennis, there will be a new world No. 1 on Monday. Elena Rybakina reached the US Open semi-finals, securing the top spot in the rankings.
 
In cycling, Matthew Brennan claimed his fifth stage win of the Vuelta at just 21 years old, becoming the youngest-ever rider to achieve the feat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef3bb6c4-acd7-11f1-b8e4-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UK6ZF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ef3bb6c4-acd7-11f1-b8e4-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7UK6ZF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">485aa40c-acd5-11f1-bde0-07d8a61eea5c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:46:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hoping to salvage midterms, Trump makes dubious pledge to give every US adult $5,000</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-hoping-to-salvage-midterms-trump-makes-dubious-pledge-to-give-every-us-adult-5-000</link><description>
President Donald Trump pledged Wednesday to send every American adult $5,000 if Republicans retain control of the House and Senate in the midterm elections, an extraordinary gambit to reverse his party's sagging fortunes in November. The dubious promise would likely cost more than $1 trillion and require congressional approval, and would further exacerbate the country’s nearly $1.8 trillion annual budget deficit and concerns about inflation. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cfe62f6a-ad00-11f1-8d03-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-100132-100815-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cfe62f6a-ad00-11f1-8d03-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-100132-100815-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d52d3572-ad00-11f1-8de3-c10e0cc4c206</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:34:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's Houthis close in on stranglehold over strategic Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-yemen-s-houthis-close-in-on-stranglehold-over-strategic-bab-el-mandeb-strait</link><description>
Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthis seized control of ​the historic port city of Mocha on Thursday, four Yemeni government military sources said, gaining further leverage over the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, one of the world's most important shipping routes. There has been an escalation in fighting between Saudi Arabia's Yemeni allies in the internationally backed government and the Houthis in recent ⁠days, creating a second theatre of war in the Iran conflict that threatens global energy supplies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d56e14fc-ad00-11f1-a56a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-120708-120841-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d56e14fc-ad00-11f1-a56a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-120708-120841-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9ee4894-ad00-11f1-b565-b9fcb0f9126c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:33:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: French President Macron addresses International Space Summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-replay-french-president-macron-addresses-international-space-summit</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday called on Europe to develop its own crewed spaceflight capability as part of a broader push to strengthen the continent's space sector. "We want Europe to demonstrate its ambition in the field of crewed spaceflight," Macron told a space summit in Paris, adding that "our European space programme remains fragile and we must step up our efforts." Watch our replay.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ef1dc5c-acf7-11f1-bc8e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-101254-103633-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ef1dc5c-acf7-11f1-bc8e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-101254-103633-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">837ba3de-acf7-11f1-9bbe-bfbc394ea958</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:30:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'AI could kill all humans': AI researcher quits Anthropic</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-ai-could-kill-all-humans-ai-researcher-quits-anthropic</link><description>
An artificial intelligence researcher who left OpenAI to join Anthropic has decided to leave the industry, accusing both US companies of "gambling with our lives" in the race to develop AI models capable of self-improvement. Anthropic safety executive Evan Hubinger backed up Coxon on X. "We really do earnestly believe AI could kill all humans!" he said, adding that he estimated that risk at more than 10 percent over the next decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/545229de-acfc-11f1-8f34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-110536-110723-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/545229de-acfc-11f1-8f34-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-110536-110723-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5942aa9a-acfc-11f1-af08-770924a1b4d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:28:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Apple's new foldable iPhone: expensive gadget or bold statement?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260910-apple-s-new-foldable-iphone-expensive-gadget-or-bold-statement</link><description>
John Ternus, Apple's new CEO, unveiled the tech giant's latest smartphone on Wednesday. The foldable iPhone Duo will go on sale on October 23rd starting at $1,999, making it the most expensive iPhone to date. The move is a bid to comfort the US company's position at the top of the global smartphone market. Also in this edition, we head to Argentina where President Javier Milei's free market approach has led to a downturn in manufacturing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4ec9844-acee-11f1-a3c6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12285369836aa26587849e75-87898272.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4ec9844-acee-11f1-a3c6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12285369836aa26587849e75-87898272.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c425b22-acee-11f1-bfc3-8d76b8e55cda</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:28:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Macron joins Sophie Adenot live from the ISS at Paris space summit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-replay-macron-joins-sophie-adenot-live-from-the-iss-at-paris-space-summit</link><description>
Speaking at the two-day International Space Summit in Paris Thursday, French President Emmanuel Macron called for "shared governance" of space in a speech urging European nations to work together to build up their joint sovereign space capabilities. He was also joined live by French astronaut Sophie Adenot, speaking from the International Space Station. Watch our replay.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af85ddba-acfb-11f1-bc87-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-104159-105131-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af85ddba-acfb-11f1-bc87-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-104159-105131-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b46002fc-acfb-11f1-aa46-bfbc394ea958</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:23:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Trump touts $5,000 payout if Republicans win</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-us-midterms-trump-touts-5-000-payout-if-republicans-win</link><description>
President Donald Trump capped the first day of his Republican Party's ​first-ever midterm convention by proposing to pay every US adult a $5,000 "Trump dividend" if his party wins November's congressional elections. Trump delivered the extraordinary overture during a primetime speech that lasted nearly two hours and firmly placed him at the center of the midterm campaign at a time when his sagging approval ratings could weigh on Republicans' chances.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50346d62-acfc-11f1-b078-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-110150-110342-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50346d62-acfc-11f1-b078-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-110150-110342-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58c91d38-acfc-11f1-9801-770924a1b4d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:21:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Provocative and blatant violation': Syria condemns Netanyahu's entry into its territory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-provocative-and-blatant-violation-syria-condemns-netanyahu-s-entry-into-its-territory</link><description>
Syria condemned Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's entry into its territory after he visited Israeli troops stationed in southern Syria on Wednesday, calling the move "provocative and a blatant violation" of its sovereignty. In southern Syria, Israeli forces have been stationed in a "security zone" since the fall of longtime ruler Bashar al-Assad in December 2024. They occupy what was previously a buffer zone patrolled by the United Nations that had separated Israeli and Syrian forces in the Israeli-occupied Golan since 1974.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01a81d14-acfd-11f1-aaac-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-110746-110920-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01a81d14-acfd-11f1-aaac-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-110746-110920-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06f7a064-acfd-11f1-ad8b-b9fcb0f9126c</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:19:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Protecting whales: Scientists seek ways to reduce ship collision risk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-protecting-whales-scientists-seek-ways-to-reduce-ship-collision-risk</link><description>
Collisions with ships are a major threat to whales in the Mediterranean, with animals killed every year after being struck by vessels. Scientists specialising in whale conservation are studying the animals’ behaviour and movements to better understand the risk and identify ways to prevent collisions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb2c7012-acfe-11f1-a84f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-111408-111544-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb2c7012-acfe-11f1-a84f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-111408-111544-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d0895b9c-acfe-11f1-b280-bfbc394ea958</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 10:17:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FRANCE 24 report: Bayeux Tapestry fever grips UK as sold-out exhibition opens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260910-france-24-report-bayeux-tapestry-fever-grips-uk-as-sold-out-exhibition-opens</link><description>
London's Bayeux Tapestry exhibition opened Thursday to a British public gripped by "mania" as the medieval artwork depicting the Norman conquest of England goes on display outside France for the first time. FRANCE 24’s Olivia Salazar-Winspear was there.
